  "note": "Matrix bundle of HQ #346: the one complete matrix run of the compact-console firmware (XSUM records). A detached run of the matrix plan (flash the image of the committed sources, then reset) followed by a COM capture on port dut (route B): 68 com_read calls of at most 12000 bytes and one GO line after each of BLOCK-END n=1 to n=30, then the reads through PANIC, the 45 s hold, RECOVERY-BOOT, the recovery setup block, the recovery occurrence and END, and one empty confirming read. Every read reported overflow_bytes 0; the bench returned 99353 bytes in total. The com_read receipts hold metadata only: their data.text is not copied by hand, the operator fills it from the runner's own records of the server responses with finalize_bundle.py --responses (runner issue #336), which checks each record against the receipt's request, bytes_read and data.hex. finalize_bundle.py then writes the frozen inputs and the console file and fills every sha256 and size of this index (the zeros here are placeholders until then). Other receipts are the tool results with private identities and host paths removed; each names what it redacts.",
